### Notes

Students are urged to acquaint themselves with the requirements of the major department in the college or university to which transfer is contemplated; and further, students are urged to consult with their counselors and advisors at VHCC in planning their academic program and electives.

To Enroll in MTH 263, Calculus I, students may complete MTH 161/MTH 162 sequence or MTH 167 or demonstrate proficiency using the following multiple measures requirement.

- be within six years of high school graduation,
- graduate from high school with at least a 3.0 average,
- complete an advanced math course in trigonometry with at least a B in that course.
